# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whitelist-style .gitignore
# Everything is ignored by default; only the allow-list rules below keep
# certain files. This keeps the repository clean for submission by
# committing ONLY the lab source files plus this README and .gitignore.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

# Ignore everything by default.
*

# Keep folders searchable so allow-list rules can apply inside them.
!*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep: lab source files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
!*.cpp      # C++ sources (Lab 1: Q1-Q15 and Lab 2: Q16-Q26)
!*.l        # Flex specifications (Lexer.l, F1_parser.l)
!*.y        # Bison grammars (F2_parser.y)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep: project documentation and ignore rules
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
!README.md
!.gitignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated / build artifacts (documented for clarity; already excluded
# by the whitelist above, these only make the intent explicit):
#   active_cpp_run.exe   -> VS Code / task build output
#   lex.yy.c             -> flex output
#   F2_parser.tab.c/.h   -> bison output
#   .vscode/             -> local, machine-specific editor config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.exe
lex.yy.c
F2_parser.tab.c
F2_parser.tab.h
.vscode/
